From fe1ab81521e17ab57b9b4d1adadd4f778e8b88f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bcup02 <55205420+bcup02@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:58:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gs): v2 projection writes entry_time/exit_time as Taipei
 local text (v0.13.3) (#8)

The v2 projection carries entry_time / exit_time as UTC ISO-8601 straight
from the ledger (opened_at / closed_at), so drained rows landed as
"2026-08-29T15:57:11Z" while every pre-v2 row is Taipei local text
"2026-08-26 0:00:49". Convert on write.

- apps_script/google_ledger_receiver.gs (canonical, deployed) + the
  reference sibling google_ledger_receiver_v2.gs, kept in sync:
  * formatSheetTime(value): UTC ISO (or any Date-parseable string) ->
    Utilities.formatDate(d, 'Asia/Taipei', 'yyyy-MM-dd H:mm:ss'). An
    already-Taipei-text value, '', or an unparseable one passes through
    unchanged and never throws -- so re-sending a row / the rewrite tool
    is safe.
  * sheetValue(): entry_time / exit_time take the new branch before the
    numeric check.
  * needsTextFormat(value): replaces the 4 inline /^[0-9]{16,}$/ checks;
    now a Taipei datetime string is also kept as verbatim text (@ format)
    so Sheets does not auto-parse it into a right-aligned Date cell, and
    it matches the left-aligned pre-v2 rows.
- payload_digest is unaffected (conversion is receiver-side, after the
  signature check); google_reconcile does not compare time columns, so
  reconcile verdicts are unchanged.
- tests/apps_script_unified_receiver_node_test.js: Utilities.formatDate
  stub (Asia/Taipei, UTC+8, no DST) + assertions that a v2 open/close
  with a UTC ISO time lands as Taipei text, and formatSheetTime
  passthrough/no-throw.
- pyproject / __init__: 0.13.2 -> 0.13.3. Release-log entry.

Consumers do NOT bump the pin (.gs is pasted manually, not imported);
v0.13.3 is only the .gs version coordinate. Re-deploying the Web App
(paste -> Manage deployments -> new version) is a separate manual step.
The ~25 already-wrong rows are fixed by a momentum-side rewrite tool
(next).

